IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgc2-sch13-small`

-- Tests for sgc2-sch13-small.l4 (the Thirteenth Schedule: small company and small group). Every expected value is written from the text of the Schedule,
-- beside the assertion. The Schedule's figures: revenue and total assets not exceeding $10 million (AT MOST 10,000,000), not more than 50 employees (AT MOST 50).
-- A year's figures are `sch 13 year figures` OF revenue, total assets, employees.

§ `Years used in the tests`

-- Named by the criteria they meet (revenue, total assets, employees): exactly at the ceilings, and one past each.
`all three met` MEANS `sch 13 year figures` OF 10000000, 10000000, 50
`revenue and assets met` MEANS `sch 13 year figures` OF 10000000, 10000000, 51
`revenue and employees met` MEANS `sch 13 year figures` OF 10000000, 10000001, 50
`assets and employees met` MEANS `sch 13 year figures` OF 10000001, 10000000, 50
`only revenue met` MEANS `sch 13 year figures` OF 10000000, 10000001, 51
`only employees met` MEANS `sch 13 year figures` OF 10000001, 10000001, 50
`none met` MEANS `sch 13 year figures` OF 10000001, 10000001, 51

§ `Paragraph 2(b): the criteria and "any 2" of them`

#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b)(i) the revenue for the financial year does not exceed $10 million` (`sch 13 year figures` OF 10000000, 0, 0) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b)(i) the revenue for the financial year does not exceed $10 million` (`sch 13 year figures` OF 10000001, 0, 0) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b)(ii) the total assets at the end of the financial year do not exceed $10 million` (`sch 13 year figures` OF 0, 10000000, 0) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b)(ii) the total assets at the end of the financial year do not exceed $10 million` (`sch 13 year figures` OF 0, 10000001, 0) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b)(iii) the company has at the end of the financial year not more than 50 employees` (`sch 13 year figures` OF 0, 0, 50) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b)(iii) the company has at the end of the financial year not more than 50 employees` (`sch 13 year figures` OF 0, 0, 51) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b) the number of the criteria the financial year satisfies` `all three met` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b) the number of the criteria the financial year satisfies` `revenue and assets met` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b) the number of the criteria the financial year satisfies` `only revenue met` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b) the number of the criteria the financial year satisfies` `none met` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `all three met` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `revenue and employees met` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `assets and employees met` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `only revenue met` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `only employees met` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b) the financial year satisfies any 2 of the criteria` `none met` EQUALS FALSE

§ `Paragraph 2: two financial years before this one`

-- (a) private throughout, and (b) any 2 criteria in each of the 2 preceding years.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` TRUE `all three met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` TRUE `revenue and assets met` `assets and employees met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a private company throughout the year: no.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` FALSE `all three met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- One of the two years fails (only 1 criterion): no. Either year.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` TRUE `only revenue met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` TRUE `all three met` `only employees met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` TRUE `none met` `none met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The two readings differ here: year 1 meets revenue and assets, year 2 meets revenue and employees. Reading (A), the one used: 2 criteria in each year, so small.
-- Reading (B), the same 2 criteria both years: only revenue holds in both, so not small.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` TRUE `revenue and assets met` `revenue and employees met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b) the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year (other reading: the same 2 criteria in both years)` TRUE `revenue and assets met` `revenue and employees met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Where both readings agree.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b) the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year (other reading: the same 2 criteria in both years)` TRUE `all three met` `revenue and assets met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b) the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year (other reading: the same 2 criteria in both years)` TRUE `only revenue met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 2(b) the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year (other reading: the same 2 criteria in both years)` FALSE `all three met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Paragraph 3: the first and second financial years after incorporation`

#ASSERT `sch 13 para 3 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` 1 TRUE `revenue and assets met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 3 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` 2 TRUE `assets and employees met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Fewer than 2 criteria, or not private throughout: no (the "if" gate).
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 3 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` 1 TRUE `only revenue met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 3 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` 2 FALSE `all three met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The third financial year (a company that has reached it), and a count below the first: outside the paragraph.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 3 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` 3 TRUE `all three met` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 3 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` 0 TRUE `all three met` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Paragraph 4: a company incorporated before 1 July 2015`

-- Incorporated 30 June 2015 (before); the first and second financial year commencing on or after 1 July 2015.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 4 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` (Date 30 6 2015) 1 TRUE `revenue and assets met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 4 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` (Date 30 6 2015) 2 TRUE `assets and employees met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 4 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` (Date 30 6 2015) 1 TRUE `only revenue met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 4 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` (Date 30 6 2015) 1 FALSE `all three met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The third financial year commencing on or after that day: outside the paragraph.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 4 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` (Date 30 6 2015) 3 TRUE `all three met` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Incorporated on 1 July 2015 itself: not "before 1 July 2015", outside the paragraph.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 4 the company qualifies as a small company from the financial year` (Date 1 7 2015) 1 TRUE `all three met` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Paragraph 6 and paragraph 5`

-- Paragraph 6: not reached the third financial year after incorporation (1 or 2), or, for a pre-1 July 2015 company, the third financial year after that date.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 6 paragraph 5 does not apply to the company` 2 (Date 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 6 paragraph 5 does not apply to the company` 3 (Date 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 6 paragraph 5 does not apply to the company` 9 (Date 30 6 2015) 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 6 paragraph 5 does not apply to the company` 9 (Date 30 6 2015) 3 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The (b) limb is for a company incorporated before 1 July 2015 only: incorporated on that day, a low count of years since 1 July 2015 does not help.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 6 paragraph 5 does not apply to the company` 9 (Date 1 7 2015) 2 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paragraph 5: a company that was not small has nothing to cease.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 5 the company ceases to be a small company from the financial year` FALSE TRUE 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 `none met` `none met` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Ceases to be a private company during the financial year: ceases (5(a)).
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 5 the company ceases to be a small company from the financial year` TRUE TRUE 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 `all three met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Fails in both preceding years: ceases (5(b), reading C1).
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 5 the company ceases to be a small company from the financial year` TRUE FALSE 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 `only revenue met` `none met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Fails in only one of the two preceding years: does not cease on reading C1 (the other reading, C2, is tested below).
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 5 the company ceases to be a small company from the financial year` TRUE FALSE 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 `only revenue met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 5 the company ceases to be a small company from the financial year` TRUE FALSE 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 `all three met` `none met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Meets the criteria in both years: does not cease.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 5 the company ceases to be a small company from the financial year` TRUE FALSE 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 `all three met` `revenue and assets met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Paragraph 6 protects a young company even where it fails both years: the second financial year after incorporation.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 5 the company ceases to be a small company from the financial year` TRUE TRUE 2 (Date 1 1 2020) 0 `none met` `none met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- And a pre-1 July 2015 company in its second financial year commencing on or after that day.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 5 the company ceases to be a small company from the financial year` TRUE FALSE 9 (Date 30 6 2015) 2 `none met` `none met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Reading C2 (not used by anything else): failing in either year.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 5(b) the company fails to satisfy any 2 of the criteria in either of the 2 preceding financial years (other reading)` `only revenue met` `all three met` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 5(b) the company fails to satisfy any 2 of the criteria in either of the 2 preceding financial years (other reading)` `all three met` `none met` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 5(b) the company fails to satisfy any 2 of the criteria in either of the 2 preceding financial years (other reading)` `all three met` `revenue and assets met` EQUALS FALSE

§ `Paragraph 1(a): the company is a small company for the financial year`

-- Arguments: the number of the financial year after incorporation; the date incorporated; the number counting from the first financial year commencing on or after 1 July 2015;
-- small for the year before; private throughout; ceases to be private in the year; this year's figures; the year before; the year before that.
-- A mature company (financial year 9, incorporated 1 January 2010), not small last year, private, with both preceding years meeting 2 criteria: qualifies under paragraph 2.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 FALSE TRUE FALSE `none met` `all three met` `revenue and assets met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not small last year, and one of the two preceding years fails: does not qualify (paragraph 2 asks both) and has nothing to continue.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 FALSE TRUE FALSE `none met` `all three met` `only revenue met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The first financial year after incorporation: paragraph 3.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 1 (Date 1 1 2026) 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE `revenue and assets met` `none met` `none met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 1 (Date 1 1 2026) 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE `only revenue met` `none met` `none met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A company incorporated before 1 July 2015, in its first financial year commencing on or after that day: paragraph 4.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 9 (Date 30 6 2015) 1 FALSE TRUE FALSE `all three met` `none met` `none met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The hysteresis of paragraphs 1(a) and 13(a): small last year, one bad preceding year only: does not cease, so still small.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 TRUE TRUE FALSE `none met` `only revenue met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Small last year, both preceding years bad: ceases (and does not qualify afresh).
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 TRUE TRUE FALSE `none met` `only revenue met` `none met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Small last year but ceases to be a private company in the year (and so is not private throughout): ceases.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 TRUE FALSE TRUE `all three met` `all three met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Small last year, in its second financial year after incorporation, with bad figures everywhere: paragraph 6 keeps it small.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 2 (Date 1 1 2025) 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE `none met` `none met` `none met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A year of paragraph 14(a): it ceased in an earlier year and qualifies again under paragraph 2 (not small last year, both preceding years good).
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 12 (Date 1 1 2010) 12 FALSE TRUE FALSE `none met` `revenue and assets met` `assets and employees met` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- A run of years for one company (incorporated 1 January 2010; all private). Year N+1's "small last year" is year N's answer.
-- Year 9: both preceding years good, not small before: small.  Year 10: last year bad, the year before good: continues.  Year 11: both bad: ceases.
-- Year 12: not small last year, both preceding years bad: not small.  Year 13: not small last year, both preceding years good again: small again (paragraph 14(a)).
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 FALSE TRUE FALSE `none met` `all three met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 10 (Date 1 1 2010) 10 TRUE TRUE FALSE `none met` `only revenue met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 11 (Date 1 1 2010) 11 TRUE TRUE FALSE `none met` `only employees met` `only revenue met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 12 (Date 1 1 2010) 12 FALSE TRUE FALSE `none met` `none met` `only employees met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(a) the company is a small company for the financial year` 13 (Date 1 1 2010) 13 FALSE TRUE FALSE `none met` `all three met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `sch 13 para 13(a) the company is a small company for the later financial year` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 13(a) the company is a small company for the later financial year` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 13(a) the company is a small company for the later financial year` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 14(a) the company may become a small company again` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 14(a) the company may become a small company again` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 14(a) the company may become a small company again` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Paragraphs 7 to 11: the small group`

#ASSERT `sch 13 para 7 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` `all three met` `revenue and assets met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 7 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` `only revenue met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 7 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` `all three met` `none met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 8 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` 1 `revenue and employees met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 8 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` 2 `only employees met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 8 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` 3 `all three met` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 9 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` (Date 30 6 2015) 1 `all three met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 9 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` (Date 30 6 2015) 2 `only revenue met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 9 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` (Date 30 6 2015) 3 `all three met` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 9 the group qualifies as a small group from the financial year` (Date 1 7 2015) 1 `all three met` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 11 paragraph 10 does not apply to the group` 2 (Date 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 11 paragraph 10 does not apply to the group` 3 (Date 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 11 paragraph 10 does not apply to the group` 9 (Date 30 6 2015) 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 11 paragraph 10 does not apply to the group` 9 (Date 30 6 2015) 3 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 10 the group ceases to be a small group from the financial year` FALSE 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 `none met` `none met` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 10 the group ceases to be a small group from the financial year` TRUE 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 `only revenue met` `none met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 10 the group ceases to be a small group from the financial year` TRUE 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 `only revenue met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 10 the group ceases to be a small group from the financial year` TRUE 2 (Date 1 1 2020) 0 `none met` `none met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 10 the group fails to satisfy any 2 of the criteria in either of the 2 preceding financial years (other reading)` `only revenue met` `all three met` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 10 the group fails to satisfy any 2 of the criteria in either of the 2 preceding financial years (other reading)` `all three met` `all three met` EQUALS FALSE
-- Paragraph 1(b): arguments: the number of the financial year after the group is formed; the date formed; the number counting from the first financial year commencing on or after 1 July 2015;
-- small last year; this year's figures; the year before; the year before that.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(b) the group is a small group for the financial year` 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 FALSE `none met` `all three met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(b) the group is a small group for the financial year` 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 FALSE `none met` `only revenue met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(b) the group is a small group for the financial year` 1 (Date 1 1 2026) 0 FALSE `revenue and assets met` `none met` `none met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(b) the group is a small group for the financial year` 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 TRUE `none met` `only revenue met` `all three met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 1(b) the group is a small group for the financial year` 9 (Date 1 1 2010) 9 TRUE `none met` `none met` `only revenue met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 13(b) the group is a small group for the later financial year` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 13(b) the group is a small group for the later financial year` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 13(b) the group is a small group for the later financial year` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 14(b) the group may become a small group again` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 14(b) the group may become a small group again` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Paragraph 12`

#ASSERT `sch 13 para 12(a) the entity is part of the group` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 12(a) the entity is part of the group` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b)(i): consolidated financial statements prepared: the figure those statements give. (b)(ii): not prepared: the aggregate of all the members.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 12(b) the consolidated total assets of the group, in Singapore dollars` TRUE 7000000 (LIST 4000000, 4000000) EQUALS 7000000
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 12(b) the consolidated total assets of the group, in Singapore dollars` FALSE 7000000 (LIST 4000000, 4000000) EQUALS 8000000
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 12(b) the consolidated total assets of the group, in Singapore dollars` FALSE 7000000 (LIST 10000000, 1) EQUALS 10000001
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 12(b) the consolidated revenue of the group, in Singapore dollars` TRUE 3000000 (LIST 1000000, 1000000) EQUALS 3000000
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 12(b) the consolidated revenue of the group, in Singapore dollars` FALSE 3000000 (LIST 1000000, 1000000, 500000) EQUALS 2500000
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 12(c) the entity is a parent for the purposes of the Schedule` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A parent that is itself a subsidiary of another entity is not a "parent" here.
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 12(c) the entity is a parent for the purposes of the Schedule` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 13 para 12(c) the entity is a parent for the purposes of the Schedule` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
